From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: robyroro <41092915+robyroro@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 10:08:19 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] installer: delete the PDF ProgID on uninstall

The installer registers {root}\Software\Classes\<PDF ProgID prefix><suffix>
for PDF documents, but uninstall deleted only the HTML and app ProgIDs;
a TODO waited for PDF support, which has since landed. Ghost's installer
smoke test found GhostPDF.<suffix> left behind in HKCU after a per-user
uninstall. The key is now deleted next to the other two.

Why: upstream bug; uninstall must leave no registration behind.
Upstream: https://crbug.com/40384442
Signed-off-by: robyroro <41092915+robyroro@users.noreply.github.com>

diff --git a/chrome/installer/setup/uninstall.cc b/chrome/installer/setup/uninstall.cc
index c0bd24ff9b8d3c8fcae09c9101ac7af89c42d5b1..ee9554d16a0785e92fc2c6e876169206f9ce6cf7 100644
--- a/chrome/installer/setup/uninstall.cc
+++ b/chrome/installer/setup/uninstall.cc
@@ -616,8 +616,11 @@ bool DeleteChromeRegistrationKeys(const InstallerState& installer_state,
                                     browser_entry_suffix);
   DeleteSoftwareClassesSubkey(root, chrome_prog_id);
 
-  // TODO(crbug.com/40384442): Delete ChromePDF ProgId once support for
-  // PDF docs has landed.
+  // Delete {root}\Software\Classes\ChromePDF, which the installer registers
+  // for PDF documents.
+  const std::wstring pdf_prog_id(install_static::GetPDFProgIdPrefix() +
+                                 browser_entry_suffix);
+  DeleteSoftwareClassesSubkey(root, pdf_prog_id);
 
   // Delete {root}\Software\Classes\<DirectLaunchUrlScheme> (e.g.,
   // google-chrome, chromium).
